+
+The drift taxonomy (synced | stale | drift | failed | pending) is correct. Without a reconciler, the dual-surface system will drift, and agents will pick whichever surface supports their current action. The rule "no stale/drift claim can authorize write-capable autonomous work" is the safety invariant, but it only works if the reconciler runs mechanically (CI job, pre-tick check) rather than relying on agent memory.
